{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias in rising markets: when the last 5–10 days show an upswing (positive slope), add an upward level shift to the whole path. In the examples, the model underpredicts by ~1–3 EUR early and ~4–7 EUR by weeks 3–4.",
    "Trend/acceleration under-capture: if momentum is positive (e.g., last price > 10-day MA), increase the forecast slope (not just the intercept). The model’s path is too flat versus the realized strong rally.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: apply an increasing uplift with forecast horizon (small adjustment days 1–5, larger days 10–30). Errors grow materially with lead time, indicating drift/structural move not reflected in the model.",
    "Lag in regime shifts: after a local bottom, the model continues to forecast low/sideways for ~1–2 weeks while the market transitions to a higher regime. Use a faster regime-switch trigger (e.g., break above recent range) to re-anchor forecasts upward.",
    "Underestimation of post-breakout persistence: when price breaks above the prior 20–30d range, reduce mean-reversion strength and assume higher persistence; the model reverts too quickly and misses sustained higher levels."
  ]
}
